# iq-transfer.env — Environment overrides for iq-transfer-watcher.service
# Deploy to: /etc/rf_worker/iq-transfer.env
# This file is loaded by iq-transfer-watcher.service via EnvironmentFile=.
#
# REQUIRED:
#   IQ_DEST — rsync destination on Brian, e.g.:
#     IQ_DEST=rf_worker@brian.local:/var/lib/rf-adapt-intel/incoming/
#
# OPTIONAL (defaults shown):
#   IQ_BW_KBPS    — rsync --bwlimit in kbps (default 2048 = 2 Mbit/s)
#   IQ_MAX_RETRIES — max rsync retry attempts per file (default 3)
#   IQ_SOURCE_DIR  — local directory containing IQ snapshots

# --- Required ---
# IQ_DEST=rf_worker@192.168.1.10:/var/lib/rf-adapt-intel/incoming/

# --- Optional ---
# IQ_BW_KBPS=2048
# IQ_MAX_RETRIES=3
# IQ_SOURCE_DIR=/var/lib/rf-adapt-intel/snapshots

# DB_DEST: rsync destination for the SQLite classifications DB (Ray→Brian).
# scripts/transfer_iq.sh syncs the DB to this destination when this is set. In watch mode it
# performs an unconditional DB sync after the initial transfer_dir sweep, then rate-limits
# subsequent event-triggered syncs via DB_SYNC_INTERVAL.
# Handles IPv6 brackets, WAL/SHM cleanup, and SQLite .backup snapshot.
# Supports IPv6: rf_worker@[2001:db8::1]:/var/lib/rf-adapt-intel/rf_adapt_intel.db
# Example IPv4: rf_worker@192.168.4.246:/var/lib/rf-adapt-intel/rf_adapt_intel.db
#DB_DEST=
